Looking at the code fragments and the Hexi library usage patterns, I need to implement serialization and deserialization functions using varint encoding with the `prefixed_varint` adaptor.

Based on the examples, I can see that:
1. Hexi uses `<<` and `>>` operators for serialization/deserialization
2. `hexi::prefixed_varint` is used for compact encoding of containers
3. The library works with buffer adaptors and binary streams

Here's the complete implementation:

```cpp
#include <hexi/hexi.h>
#include <vector>
#include <string>
#include <cstdint>
#include <span>

struct CompactPacket {
    uint32_t packet_id;
    std::vector<std::string> tags;
    std::string data;
};

std::vector<uint8_t> serialize_compact_packet(const CompactPacket& packet) {
    // Create a buffer to hold serialized data
    std::vector<uint8_t> buffer;

    // Create a buffer adaptor with empty initialization
    hexi::pmc::buffer_adaptor adaptor(buffer, hexi::init_empty);

    // Create a binary stream for serialization
    hexi::pmc::binary_stream stream(adaptor);

    // Serialize packet_id as varint
    stream << hexi::varint(packet.packet_id);

    // Serialize tags vector with prefixed_varint for compact encoding
    stream << hexi::prefixed_varint(packet.tags);

    // Serialize data string with prefixed_varint for compact encoding
    stream << hexi::prefixed_varint(packet.data);

    return buffer;
}

CompactPacket deserialize_compact_packet(const std::span<const uint8_t> buffer) {
    CompactPacket packet;

    // Create a buffer read adaptor from the span
    hexi::pmc::buffer_read_adaptor adaptor(buffer);

    // Create a binary stream for deserialization
    hexi::pmc::binary_stream stream(adaptor);

    // Deserialize packet_id using varint
    stream >> hexi::varint(packet.packet_id);

    // Deserialize tags vector with prefixed_varint
    stream >> hexi::prefixed_varint(packet.tags);

    // Deserialize data string with prefixed_varint
    stream >> hexi::prefixed_varint(packet.data);

    return packet;
}
```

